{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "Semgrep OSS",
          "semanticVersion": "1.95.0",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "python.flask.security.audit.sql-injection",
              "name": "sql-injection",
              "shortDescription": { "text": "SQL injection via unsanitized user input" },
              "fullDescription": { "text": "User-controlled data is passed directly to a SQL query without parameterization. An attacker can manipulate the query to read, modify, or delete arbitrary database records." },
              "helpUri": "https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.security.audit.sql-injection",
              "help": {
                "text": "Use parameterized queries.",
                "markdown": "User-controlled input reaches a SQL sink without sanitization.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [OWASP SQL Injection](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/SQL_Injection)\n - [CWE-89](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/89.html)\n\n## Fix\nReplace string concatenation with parameterized queries:\n```python\ncursor.execute(\"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id=%s\", (user_id,))\n```"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": { "level": "error" },
              "properties": {
                "tags": ["CWE-89: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command", "security", "HIGH CONFIDENCE"],
                "security-severity": "9.1",
                "problem.severity": "error",
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "generic.secrets.security.hardcoded-aws-key",
              "name": "hardcoded-aws-key",
              "shortDescription": { "text": "Hardcoded AWS access key" },
              "fullDescription": { "text": "An AWS access key is hardcoded in the source file. If this file is committed to version control or exposed, the credentials can be used to access AWS resources." },
              "helpUri": "https://semgrep.dev/r/generic.secrets.security.hardcoded-aws-key",
              "help": {
                "text": "Use environment variables or a secrets manager.",
                "markdown": "AWS credentials are hardcoded in source code.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [CWE-798](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/798.html)\n - [AWS Secrets Manager](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/intro.html)\n\n## Fix\nRemove the hardcoded key and load it from the environment:\n```python\nAWS_SECRET_KEY = os.environ[\"AWS_SECRET_KEY\"]\n```"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": { "level": "error" },
              "properties": {
                "tags": ["CWE-798: Use of Hard-coded Credentials", "security", "HIGH CONFIDENCE"],
                "security-severity": "9.8",
                "problem.severity": "error",
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "python.lang.security.audit.dangerous-system-call",
              "name": "dangerous-system-call",
              "shortDescription": { "text": "OS command injection via user-controlled input" },
              "fullDescription": { "text": "User-controlled data flows into os.system() or subprocess with shell=True. An attacker can inject arbitrary shell commands." },
              "helpUri": "https://semgrep.dev/r/python.lang.security.audit.dangerous-system-call",
              "help": {
                "text": "Use subprocess with a list argument.",
                "markdown": "Dangerous system call reached with user input.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [CWE-78](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/78.html)\n - [OWASP Command Injection](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Command_Injection)\n\n## Fix\nAvoid shell=True and pass arguments as a list:\n```python\nsubprocess.run([\"convert\", \"-resize\", size, \"output.png\"], shell=False)\n```"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": { "level": "error" },
              "properties": {
                "tags": ["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command", "security", "HIGH CONFIDENCE"],
                "security-severity": "8.5",
                "problem.severity": "error",
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "python.requests.security.ssrf-injection",
              "name": "ssrf-injection",
              "shortDescription": { "text": "Server-side request forgery (SSRF)" },
              "fullDescription": { "text": "A URL derived from user input is passed to requests.get() or similar. An attacker can direct the server to make requests to internal network resources or cloud metadata endpoints." },
              "helpUri": "https://semgrep.dev/r/python.requests.security.ssrf-injection",
              "defaultConfiguration": { "level": "error" },
              "properties": {
                "tags": ["CWE-918: Server-Side Request Forgery", "security", "MEDIUM CONFIDENCE"],
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "problem.severity": "error",
                "precision": "medium"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "javascript.browser.security.dom-xss",
              "name": "dom-xss",
              "shortDescription": { "text": "DOM-based cross-site scripting (XSS)" },
              "fullDescription": { "text": "Unsanitized user-controlled data is written to innerHTML. An attacker can inject arbitrary HTML and execute JavaScript in the victim's browser." },
              "helpUri": "https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.browser.security.dom-xss",
              "defaultConfiguration": { "level": "warning" },
              "properties": {
                "tags": ["CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation", "security", "MEDIUM CONFIDENCE"],
                "security-severity": "6.1",
                "problem.severity": "warning",
                "precision": "medium"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "python.lang.security.audit.path-traversal",
              "name": "path-traversal",
              "shortDescription": { "text": "Path traversal via unsanitized filename" },
              "fullDescription": { "text": "A filename from user input is joined with a base directory without sanitization. An attacker can use '../' sequences to escape the intended directory and read arbitrary files." },
              "helpUri": "https://semgrep.dev/r/python.lang.security.audit.path-traversal",
              "help": {
                "text": "Validate and sanitize file paths.",
                "markdown": "User-controlled path reaches os.path.join or open without validation.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [CWE-22](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/22.html)\n\n## Fix\nUse os.path.realpath and verify the result stays within the allowed directory:\n```python\nsafe_path = os.path.realpath(os.path.join(BASE_DIR, filename))\nif not safe_path.startswith(BASE_DIR):\n    abort(403)\n```"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": { "level": "warning" },
              "properties": {
                "tags": ["CWE-22: Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory", "security", "MEDIUM CONFIDENCE"],
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "problem.severity": "warning",
                "precision": "medium"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "python.lang.security.weak-cryptography.use-of-md5",
              "name": "use-of-md5",
              "shortDescription": { "text": "Use of MD5 for cryptographic hashing" },
              "fullDescription": { "text": "MD5 is a cryptographically broken hash function. Do not use it for passwords, integrity checks, or any security-sensitive purpose." },
              "helpUri": "https://semgrep.dev/r/python.lang.security.weak-cryptography.use-of-md5",
              "defaultConfiguration": { "level": "warning" },
              "properties": {
                "tags": ["CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm", "security", "LOW CONFIDENCE"],
                "security-severity": "4.5",
                "problem.severity": "warning",
                "precision": "low"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "generic.nginx.security.missing-security-header",
              "name": "missing-security-header",
              "shortDescription": { "text": "Missing HTTP security response header" },
              "fullDescription": { "text": "The nginx server block does not set a recommended HTTP security header. Missing headers can expose users to clickjacking, MIME-sniffing, and XSS attacks." },
              "helpUri": "https://semgrep.dev/r/generic.nginx.security.missing-security-header",
              "defaultConfiguration": { "level": "warning" },
              "properties": {
                "tags": ["CWE-693: Protection Mechanism Failure", "security", "MEDIUM CONFIDENCE"],
                "security-severity": "5.0",
                "problem.severity": "warning",
                "precision": "medium"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "python.flask.security.audit.insecure-cookie",
              "name": "insecure-cookie",
              "shortDescription": { "text": "Cookie missing Secure and HttpOnly flags" },
              "fullDescription": { "text": "The session cookie is set without the Secure or HttpOnly flag. Without Secure the cookie may be sent over plaintext HTTP; without HttpOnly it is accessible to JavaScript." },
              "helpUri": "https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.security.audit.insecure-cookie",
              "help": {
                "text": "Set Secure and HttpOnly flags on cookies.",
                "markdown": "Cookie set without security flags.\n\n## Fix\nPass `secure=True, httponly=True` to set_cookie:\n```python\nresponse.set_cookie('session', token, secure=True, httponly=True, samesite='Lax')\n```"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": { "level": "note" },
              "properties": {
                "tags": ["CWE-1004: Sensitive Cookie Without HttpOnly Flag", "security", "LOW CONFIDENCE"],
                "security-severity": "3.5",
                "problem.severity": "note",
                "precision": "low"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "python.flask.security.audit.debug-enabled",
              "name": "debug-enabled",
              "shortDescription": { "text": "Flask debug mode enabled in production code" },
              "fullDescription": { "text": "app.run(debug=True) enables the Werkzeug debugger and reloader. If reached in production this exposes an interactive Python console to any user who triggers an exception." },
              "helpUri": "https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.security.audit.debug-enabled",
              "defaultConfiguration": { "level": "note" },
              "properties": {
                "tags": ["CWE-489: Active Debug Code", "security", "LOW CONFIDENCE"],
                "security-severity": "3.0",
                "problem.severity": "note",
                "precision": "low"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "generic.web.security.missing-rate-limiting",
              "name": "missing-rate-limiting",
              "shortDescription": { "text": "Sensitive endpoint lacks rate limiting" },
              "fullDescription": { "text": "The login or authentication endpoint does not appear to enforce rate limiting. Without it the endpoint is vulnerable to credential-stuffing and brute-force attacks." },
              "helpUri": "https://semgrep.dev/r/generic.web.security.missing-rate-limiting",
              "defaultConfiguration": { "level": "none" },
              "properties": {
                "tags": ["security", "LOW CONFIDENCE"],
                "precision": "low"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
